node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
.env
*.log
.DS_Store
.gstack/
.codegraph/
.peaks/_runtime/
# slice 2.5.0 sub-fix C: peaks playwright start session records.
# The directory lives under _runtime/ so it is already covered by
# the rule above; this explicit line documents the intent for
# future readers (and survives a future rule refactor).
.peaks/_runtime/playwright-sessions/
.peaks/_dogfood/
.peaks/_sub_agents/
.peaks/audit/
.peaks/DS_Store/
.peaks/system/       # sub-agent dispatch prompts (rd-prompt-*.txt, qa-prompt-*.txt); ephemeral session state, mirror of _sub_agents/
# Defensive: .peaks/runtime/ (no underscore) is a wrong-path pattern; canonical is .peaks/_runtime/
.peaks/runtime/
# Per-project user state (spec §8.4); regenerated by preferences-service on first read.
.peaks/preferences.json
# Auto-generated upgrade record from `peaks upgrade --to 2.0`; per-installation artifact, not source-of-truth.
.peaks/memory/upgrade-2.0-*.md
# Loop Engineering dogfood ephemeral state DB (created by tests/integration/dogfood-loop-engineering-crystallization.test.ts).
# The asset layer has been crystallized into .peaks/memory/2026-07-07-loop-engineering-first-crystallization.md;
# the raw SQLite DB is per-installation and not source-of-truth.
.peaks/state.db
# Defense (slice 2026-06-22-top-level-change-id-cleanup): no YYYY-MM-DD-prefixed
# directories are allowed at `.peaks/` top level. change-id / session-id style
# dirs must live under `.peaks/_runtime/<sid>/` (gitignored) — never as siblings.
# Matches: .peaks/2026-06-22-cc-connect-orphan-cleanup/, .peaks/2026-06-21-... etc.
# Does NOT match: .peaks/_runtime/2026-06-22-session-14216e/ (underscore prefix).
.peaks/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-*/
# Dogfood / scratch test runners; ephemeral, never source-of-truth.
.tmp/
.pack-cache/
*.tgz

.playwright-mcp/
# superpowers brainstorm ephemeral state — per-run process state (port/pid/instance id/stop marker).
# content/*.html under <session-id>/ stays tracked (it is the user's brainstorm artifact catalog).
.superpowers/brainstorm/
tmp-mut-test/
tmp-shared-channel-*/
**/.tmp-mut-test/
**/.tmp-shared-channel-*/
# BDD reporter test fixtures — ephemeral, generated at runtime.
# Deliberately under tests/fixtures/ (outside the `tests/unit/**/*.test.ts`
# collection glob and outside the tsc program's `tests/**/*.ts`) so a fixture
# that is deleted mid-run cannot be collected by vitest or read by tsc.
tests/fixtures/bdd-reporter-tmp/
# best-practice-scan artifacts — ephemeral, written to <project>/best-practice/<date>-<intent>.md.
# The CLI's own help says "(gitignored)"; this is the rule that makes that true.
#
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. A bare `best-practice/` is read the way .gitignore
# reads it everywhere else — a trailing slash with no inner slash matches a
# DIRECTORY OF THAT NAME AT ANY DEPTH — so it also swallowed `src/services/best-practice/`
# and `tests/unit/best-practice/`: 6 tracked source files, invisible to `git status`,
# to `prettier --check` and to `pnpm format`. Prettier reads .gitignore by default,
# so `prettier --check` printed "All matched files use Prettier code style!" while
# never reading those files at all.
#
# Third instance of this class in this repository (cf. eslint's `ignorePatterns:
# ['skills/']` swallowing src/services/skills/, and the codegraph excludes). The
# intent here was always the ONE top-level artifact directory, so anchor it.
/best-practice/

# >>> peaks-loop managed snippet (slice 2.0.1-bug3) — do not edit by hand
# Consumer-project .claude/settings.local.json: written by `peaks workspace init`
# to bypass Claude Code [Fact-Forcing Gate] for .peaks/** writes. Local-only.
.claude/settings.local.json
# Offline template copy (.peaks/.claude-settings-template.json): written by
# `peaks workspace init` as a manual-recovery anchor. The source-of-truth is
# peaks-loop's own `buildClaudeSettingsLocalJson()` — NOT this committed copy.
# Gitignored so the init flow's drift-driven refresh does not show up as
# "modified" in `git status` on every release bump. Recovery path: re-run
# `peaks workspace init` to regenerate; or copy from peaks-loop source.
# Both patterns below are PROJECT-ROOT-relative, so this snippet must land
# in the root .gitignore — see `upsertPeaksGitignoreSnippet`.
.peaks/.claude-settings-template.json
# Codegraph rollback copy (A3, 2026-09-17). Every `peaks codegraph init` /
# `repair-exclude` / `repair-index` / pre-dispatch preflight / post-slice
# auto-refresh copies `.codegraph/config.json` here before rewriting it, so
# this file is LOCAL CHURN: a committed one is silently replaced by the next
# repair. Upstream's own `.codegraph/.gitignore` does not cover it (it names
# *.db / *.db-wal / *.db-shm, cache/, *.log and .dirty only) and `.codegraph/`
# is NOT ignored wholesale downstream, so without this line a consumer project
# commits a file peaks-loop rewrites under it.
#
# ONLY the backup, never `config.json` itself: upstream deliberately keeps
# that config committable (it is a project's include/exclude policy, and
# committing it is how a team shares it), so ignoring it would hide a file
# people mean to commit. A rollback copy is the opposite kind of file.
.codegraph/config.json.bak
# <<< peaks-loop managed snippet
